%S A399921 1,1527,6487,32047,34207,42127,51847,56887,59911,62287,64807,65311,
%T A399921 24415560,24787020,25506936,26292390,26520648,26692860,27557082,
%U A399921 29885240,31723160,31732540,31881290,33141160,42456735,44354037
%N A399921 Numbers k such that psi(k) = phi(k) + omega(k)^10.
%C A399921 The Python program available at the linked GitHub repository computes the solutions to psi(k) = phi(k) + omega(k)^m for arbitrary positive integer values of m. For this sequence, use m = 10.
%H A399921 S. I. Dimitrov, <a href="https://github.com/Stoyan16/Numbers-k-such-that-psi-k-phi-k-omega-k-9/blob/main/A401530">Python program</a> (GitHub).
%e A399921 1527 is a term since psi(1527) = 2040 = 1016 + 2^10 = phi(1527) + omega(1527)^10.
%o A399921 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); prod(i=1, #f~, (f[i, 1]+1) * f[i, 1]^(f[i, 2]-1)) - eulerphi(f) == omega(f)^10; } \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Nov 04 2026
%Y A399921 Cf. A000010, A001221, A001615, A401530.
%K A399921 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A399921 1,2
%A A399921 _S. I. Dimitrov_, Nov 04 2026
